# {display_name}

{description}

A ModeratorIM **app** — a path-discovered addon. It exposes a `manifest` at its module root and
imports **only** `moderatorim.sdk` (never `moderatorim.core`); it talks to core at runtime through
injected handles (`ctx.store`, `ctx.authz`, `ctx.can`, the event bus).

## Conventions

- Tables are declared with the `{name}_` prefix (e.g. `{name}_users`), validated at boot.
- Permissions and roles live in the `{name}.*` namespace.
- Fold by domain: `moderatorim generate model <domain>` creates `<domain>/model.py`, and
  `generate service/routes/view <domain>` add to that same domain package.

## Layout

```
{name}/
  __init__.py        # exposes `manifest`
  manifest.py        # the unit's self-declaration
  tests/             # hermetic tests (run with pytest)
```
